{{right|''Capt. John Smith'', Works, II. 195.}}
<poem>Here plots of sparkling water tremble bright
With thousand thousand ''twinkling'' points of light.</poem>
{{right|''Wordsworth'', Evening Walk.}}
<poem>I see his gray eyes ''twinkle'' yet
At his own jest.</poem>
{{right|''Tennyson'', Miller’s Daughter.}}}}

'''II.''' ''trans.'' '''1.''' To open and shut rapidly; wink; blink.

